### 1. Get all patients (newest 50)
GET http://localhost:3000/patients

### 2. Get one patient from the real database
GET http://localhost:3000/patients/1

### 3. Create a new patient → 201
POST http://localhost:3000/patients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Nurul Huda",
  "icNumber": "950101-10-8888",
}

### 4. Bad data → 400
POST http://localhost:3000/patients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "",
  "icNumber": "123",
}

### 5. IC already in database (Lim from Lesson 12) → 409
POST http://localhost:3000/patients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Copy Cat",
  "icNumber": "700707-07-7777",
}

### 6. Sneaky extra field → 400
POST http://localhost:3000/patients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Hacker",
  "icNumber": "990909-09-9999",
  "isAdmin": true
}

### 7. Today's queue
GET http://localhost:3000/appointments/today

### 8. Book Faridah (use HER id from the patients page)
POST http://localhost:3000/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "patientId": 20011,
  "reason": "Headache"
}

### 9. Book a patient that doesn't exist → 404
POST http://localhost:3000/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "patientId": 999999
}

### 10. Call appointment (change the id to one from #7)
PATCH http://localhost:3000/appointments/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "called"
}

### 11. Invalid status → 400
PATCH http://localhost:3000/appointments/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "sleeping"
}

### 12. Find patient by IC (returning patient)
GET http://localhost:3000/patients/by-ic/850612-10-1234

### 13. Unknown IC → 404 (new patient)
GET http://localhost:3000/patients/by-ic/990101-01-0101